From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:17:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 064/117] regulator: add Apple PMIC touchscreen supply driver

The D111 touchscreen power sequence depends on a core switch in Adelyn and
a high-voltage switch in Chestnut. Driving those PMIC registers from the
touchscreen consumer would couple two devices, bypass regulator ownership
and make unbind or error rollback difficult to balance.

Add a platform regulator driver with per-compatible regulator descriptors
for the two physical rails. The driver obtains the parent-owned regmap,
registers through devm_regulator_register(), and uses the standard
regmap-backed enable, disable and state operations. Register addresses and
masks remain in match data rather than device tree.

The regulator core therefore owns consumer references and sequencing,
while managed registration covers probe failure and removal without a
generic MFD, regmap or regulator-core special case. Probe rejects missing
match data or a parent without a regmap before exposing a regulator. The
complete series built Image.gz, DTBs and modules, and the D111 hardware
test exercised both rails through a successful apple-z2 probe with no
regulator errors. This patch was checked with checkpatch.pl --strict.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: cb07f8756ea0a58701cde87194bd11f2ca2aa1a6
